Similarly, if you
have a warehouse,

00:12:43.750 --> 00:12:46.390
and you have employees
working in the warehouse who

00:12:46.390 --> 00:12:48.910
need to have rugged hand-held
devices as data capture

00:12:48.910 --> 00:12:51.700
devices, the Honeywell
device or the Zebra device

00:12:51.700 --> 00:12:53.620
are probably right
devices that you may

00:12:53.620 --> 00:12:55.900
want to select and consider.

00:12:55.900 --> 00:12:59.920
Chrome OS also offers a
variety of different solutions

00:12:59.920 --> 00:13:01.446
that we have built,
building on top

00:13:01.446 --> 00:13:03.320
of both the Chrome and
the Android platforms.

00:13:03.320 --> 00:13:05.800
However at Google, we have
been building solutions

00:13:05.800 --> 00:13:08.140
around the Chrome platform.

00:13:08.140 --> 00:13:10.990
The three specific solutions
that we have been building

00:13:10.990 --> 00:13:13.780
are public sessions,
digital signage,

00:13:13.780 --> 00:13:19.660
and single purpose kiosks, which
I will talk about in a bit.

00:13:19.660 --> 00:13:21.910
So first to describe
each of these three use

00:13:21.910 --> 00:13:25.240
cases, one, digital signs.

00:13:25.240 --> 00:13:28.000
So I'll walk through
all these three examples

00:13:28.000 --> 00:13:33.370
also in terms of a retail
setting and how this works.

00:13:33.370 --> 00:13:35.950
So consider again,
you're a retailer.

00:13:35.950 --> 00:13:41.320
And you have Mary who is
your most loyal shopper, who

00:13:41.320 --> 00:13:44.140
has walked into your store.

00:13:44.140 --> 00:13:47.920
And your store is completely
outfitted with digital signs,

00:13:47.920 --> 00:13:51.790
smart digital signs which are
showing promotional content

00:13:51.790 --> 00:13:54.730
prices and a lot of
promotional information, which

00:13:54.730 --> 00:13:58.130
keep changing with
the time of the day.

00:13:58.130 --> 00:14:02.650
So now the intelligence
sign recognizes Mary.

00:14:02.650 --> 00:14:06.330
And it identifies
her as a woman.

00:14:06.330 --> 00:14:10.030
And she's about, say,
30, 35 years old.

00:14:10.030 --> 00:14:14.410
And then as Mary continues
to walk through the store,

00:14:14.410 --> 00:14:17.260
it's providing her
with the right content,

00:14:17.260 --> 00:14:20.530
relevant content, or
maybe access to coupons,

00:14:20.530 --> 00:14:23.080
or access to other type
of promotional links

00:14:23.080 --> 00:14:26.290
that she can take advantage of,
which makes her entire shopping

00:14:26.290 --> 00:14:29.590
experience to be truly
personalized and delightful.

00:14:29.590 --> 00:14:31.900
So how does this all work?

00:14:31.900 --> 00:14:36.280
We promote this kind of a
solution using Chrome OS

00:14:36.280 --> 00:14:37.190
devices.

00:14:37.190 --> 00:14:41.440
So you can actually pair
a screen, a monitor,

00:14:41.440 --> 00:14:42.490
with a Chromebox.

00:14:42.490 --> 00:14:44.370
And you can get a smart screen.

00:14:44.370 --> 00:14:48.880
And Chrome OS inherently
supports beacon technology

00:14:48.880 --> 00:14:51.300
from Google, which is
called the Eddystone Beacon.

00:14:51.300 --> 00:14:53.820
So it comes in with
a built in sensor.

00:14:53.820 --> 00:14:56.470
And with Eddystone
Beacons, the way it works

00:14:56.470 --> 00:15:00.820
is the screen would now
broadcast Eddystone URLs.

00:15:00.820 --> 00:15:03.610
And any user-- in
this case Mary--

00:15:03.610 --> 00:15:05.890
when she's walking
around and walking about

00:15:05.890 --> 00:15:08.980
to sign her smartphone
picks it up.

00:15:08.980 --> 00:15:12.370
And then she receives
notifications in her smartphone

00:15:12.370 --> 00:15:15.040
where she can actually
click the appropriate links

00:15:15.040 --> 00:15:17.380
to access coupons or
promotional content

00:15:17.380 --> 00:15:19.120
or anything of that sort.

00:15:19.120 --> 00:15:21.880
So all of this is technology
that is possible today.

00:15:21.880 --> 00:15:23.380
In addition, when
I spoke earlier

00:15:23.380 --> 00:15:27.840
that the smart sign is able to
recognize Mary and determine

00:15:27.840 --> 00:15:29.980
that she's a woman,
and she's probably

00:15:29.980 --> 00:15:34.000
about 30 to 35 years old, that
is possible using integrations

00:15:34.000 --> 00:15:35.582
with the Cloud Vision API.

00:15:35.582 --> 00:15:37.540
So you can integrate with
the Cloud Vision API.

00:15:37.540 --> 00:15:39.880
And that can detect
even if Mary--

00:15:39.880 --> 00:15:41.410
it can detect her emotions.

00:15:41.410 --> 00:15:42.730
It can detect her moods.

00:15:42.730 --> 00:15:46.480
It could say, Mary is probably
not very happy right now.

00:15:46.480 --> 00:15:47.740
Or Mary is sad.

00:15:47.740 --> 00:15:49.540
And based on what
her moods are, it

00:15:49.540 --> 00:15:52.090
can also provide relevant
contextual information

00:15:52.090 --> 00:15:55.840
that gets passed on
to her smartphone.

00:15:55.840 --> 00:15:57.310
The second most
important solution

00:15:57.310 --> 00:15:59.950
that we have been building
is called a single app kiosk.

00:15:59.950 --> 00:16:04.000
And again in this case, Mary
now has identified the items

00:16:04.000 --> 00:16:05.470
that she wants to purchase.

00:16:05.470 --> 00:16:07.060
And she can go and
check them out.

00:16:07.060 --> 00:16:11.001
So she can use a Chromebase
to actually go and check out

00:16:11.001 --> 00:16:11.500
the items.

00:16:11.500 --> 00:16:13.960
It could be a self-service
check out kiosk.

00:16:13.960 --> 00:16:16.000
Or it could be a
kiosk where she's been

00:16:16.000 --> 00:16:18.650
assisted by a sales associate.

00:16:18.650 --> 00:16:21.670
And lastly in the
final scenario,

00:16:21.670 --> 00:16:25.030
this is a situation where
at the time of checking out,

00:16:25.030 --> 00:16:29.590
Mary is asked if she wants
to sign up for a credit card.

00:16:29.590 --> 00:16:32.820
How many of you, when you go
to a store, have been asked,

00:16:32.820 --> 00:16:34.534
do you want to sign
up for a credit card?

00:16:34.534 --> 00:16:36.450
Or do you want to sign
up for a line of credit

00:16:36.450 --> 00:16:37.280
from this retailer?

00:16:37.280 --> 00:16:39.230
It's a very common scenario.

00:16:39.230 --> 00:16:40.750
So here Mary is
asked to do that.

00:16:40.750 --> 00:16:41.650
And she says, yes.

00:16:41.650 --> 00:16:42.790
She wants to do it.

00:16:42.790 --> 00:16:45.280
So she can actually
use this session.

00:16:45.280 --> 00:16:46.710
It's called Public sessions.

00:16:46.710 --> 00:16:48.970
We have built this on Chrome OS.

00:16:48.970 --> 00:16:51.220
And with Public
sessions, Mary does not

00:16:51.220 --> 00:16:53.110
have to sign in with
a Google account.

00:16:53.110 --> 00:16:55.540
In fact, she doesn't have
to sign up with any account.

00:16:55.540 --> 00:16:57.670
She just gets into the session.

00:16:57.670 --> 00:16:59.800
It's completely private,
completely secure,

00:16:59.800 --> 00:17:01.374
completely incognito.

00:17:01.374 --> 00:17:03.040
And within this
session, she can quickly

00:17:03.040 --> 00:17:04.780
fill out the application.

00:17:04.780 --> 00:17:06.099
And then she's done.

00:17:06.099 --> 00:17:09.369
And once she exits the session,
all data on the session

00:17:09.369 --> 00:17:10.450
is completely removed.

00:17:10.450 --> 00:17:12.190
The session is ephemeral.

00:17:12.190 --> 00:17:14.500
Any data in the device
is completely removed

00:17:14.500 --> 00:17:17.440
and wiped out, making this to
be a truly incognito session.

00:17:20.140 --> 00:17:23.680
So as your deployment scales,
you start with one device.

00:17:23.680 --> 00:17:27.000
And now you want to scale
out to hundreds of devices

00:17:27.000 --> 00:17:29.080
or even thousands of
devices and also want

00:17:29.080 --> 00:17:31.680
to scale out to many
geographic locations.

00:17:31.680 --> 00:17:34.495
You may want to be able
to manage these devices.

00:17:34.495 --> 00:17:36.120
As I mentioned in
the earlier scenario,

00:17:36.120 --> 00:17:38.203
you wouldn't want to have
a situation where you're

00:17:38.203 --> 00:17:43.290
sending out a technician or an
engineer to every remote site

00:17:43.290 --> 00:17:45.990
and have that technician
fix the problems.

00:17:45.990 --> 00:17:50.220
But instead you would probably
want to remotely manage

00:17:50.220 --> 00:17:51.090
your devices.

00:17:51.090 --> 00:17:53.879
You want to remotely
manage your policies

00:17:53.879 --> 00:17:56.170
and push the configurations
through a Remote Management

00:17:56.170 --> 00:17:57.330
Console.

00:17:57.330 --> 00:18:01.470
So Google offers a web-based
Remote Management Console

00:18:01.470 --> 00:18:04.170
to manage your
Chrome OS endpoints.

00:18:04.170 --> 00:18:07.040
And it's called the Chrome
Device Management Console.

00:18:07.040 --> 00:18:09.990
And with the Chrome
Device Management Console,

00:18:09.990 --> 00:18:11.700
you can do a ton
of stuff really.

00:18:11.700 --> 00:18:15.990
So you can monitor the
health of the devices.

00:18:15.990 --> 00:18:18.600
As an IT administrator,
you can push policies.

00:18:18.600 --> 00:18:21.870
You can detect
connectivity status,

00:18:21.870 --> 00:18:25.710
which devices are online,
which devices are offline.

00:18:25.710 --> 00:18:28.200
You can also get to
remote screen grabs.

00:18:28.200 --> 00:18:30.354
You can schedule automatic
restarts and reboots.

00:18:30.354 --> 00:18:32.520
We'll go through a quick
demo towards the end, where

00:18:32.520 --> 00:18:34.770
you can see some of these,
some of this functionality

00:18:34.770 --> 00:18:37.240
in action.

00:18:37.240 --> 00:18:40.930
And similar options also
exist with Android devices

00:18:40.930 --> 00:18:42.420
that need to be managed.

00:18:42.420 --> 00:18:44.920
And we work with a number of
third party partners like SOTI,

00:18:44.920 --> 00:18:47.410
and MobileIron, and AirWatch,
who definitely provide

00:18:47.410 --> 00:18:48.670
similar offerings as well.

00:18:51.772 --> 00:18:53.730
And the most important
thing, and the advantage

00:18:53.730 --> 00:18:56.640
of the Chrome and the
Android platform ecosystem,

00:18:56.640 --> 00:19:00.580
is the robust app ecosystem
that is out there.

00:19:00.580 --> 00:19:04.460
So you have a ton of
applications out there.

00:19:04.460 --> 00:19:07.170
So first of all, you have
access to over 1 million apps

00:19:07.170 --> 00:19:08.790
on Google Play.

00:19:08.790 --> 00:19:12.630
You also get access to several
Chrome content management apps.

00:19:12.630 --> 00:19:18.930
So you have apps like SCALAR,
Wondersign, Appspace, Skykit.

00:19:18.930 --> 00:19:22.140
All of these are rich
HTML5 content apps

00:19:22.140 --> 00:19:27.010
that can be deployed on a Chrome
media player, on a Chromebox.

00:19:27.010 --> 00:19:29.340
And you can actually convert
that into a digital sign.

00:19:29.340 --> 00:19:31.048
You can transform it
into a digital sign.

00:19:35.480 --> 00:19:38.850
And today I'm also really
happy to announce the support

00:19:38.850 --> 00:19:40.500
for Android Kiosk apps.

00:19:40.500 --> 00:19:43.380
So you can actually
run Android Kiosk apps

00:19:43.380 --> 00:19:46.920
on any one of our list
of supported devices

00:19:46.920 --> 00:19:49.500
where Android apps
are enabled today.

00:19:49.500 --> 00:19:51.450
We've got about four
devices out there.

00:19:51.450 --> 00:19:53.670
In addition, these
two devices out here

00:19:53.670 --> 00:19:57.840
are our hero devices for
purpose bolt, the Chromebox Mini

00:19:57.840 --> 00:19:59.100
and the Chromebase Mini.

00:19:59.100 --> 00:20:02.790
These two devices will also
support Android Kiosk apps.

00:20:02.790 --> 00:20:05.760
So with this, you can actually
get a fully locked down,

00:20:05.760 --> 00:20:07.540
immersive experience.

00:20:07.540 --> 00:20:10.690
You can use the same Chrome
Device Management Console

00:20:10.690 --> 00:20:12.920
to push down Chrome apps.

00:20:12.920 --> 00:20:16.620
And you can also push down
the Android apps from Play.

00:20:16.620 --> 00:20:18.280
So here is an example.

00:20:18.280 --> 00:20:22.500
We worked with a
retailer, with a partner

00:20:22.500 --> 00:20:25.100
in Australia called CrowdDJ.

00:20:25.100 --> 00:20:27.720
And they have a very
cool Android app that

00:20:27.720 --> 00:20:29.700
is available in Google Play.

00:20:29.700 --> 00:20:34.290
And this app actually allows
customers to control the beat.

00:20:34.290 --> 00:20:38.010
They allow customers to
select the tracks from Spotify

00:20:38.010 --> 00:20:43.020
that they want their customers
in gyms or in event venues

00:20:43.020 --> 00:20:45.990
or in restaurants to
actually have access to.

00:20:45.990 --> 00:20:48.912
So we can actually
now run this app.

00:20:48.912 --> 00:20:51.120
This is the Android app that
is downloaded from Play.

00:20:51.120 --> 00:20:54.520
And it runs on this device,
on the Chromebase Mini.

00:20:54.520 --> 00:20:56.960
So they actually
have this piloting

00:20:56.960 --> 00:20:59.050
in a bunch of
centers in Australia.

00:20:59.050 --> 00:21:03.360
Similarly education,
one of the biggest use

00:21:03.360 --> 00:21:08.100
cases for Kiosk apps is
running assessments, testing

00:21:08.100 --> 00:21:10.230
applications in schools.

00:21:10.230 --> 00:21:13.470
And with this functionality,
a lot of schools

00:21:13.470 --> 00:21:15.870
can actually deploy
Android-based testing

00:21:15.870 --> 00:21:17.940
applications, which
can then be locked down

00:21:17.940 --> 00:21:21.360
to the device to create a
full immersive experience.

00:21:21.360 --> 00:21:26.760
So I wanted to go
through a quick demo of--

00:21:26.760 --> 00:21:30.484
maybe we can do a quick demo
here of turning off the device,

00:21:30.484 --> 00:21:32.650
so that you can actually
see how the app looks like.

00:21:32.650 --> 00:21:34.410
So we have two devices.

00:21:34.410 --> 00:21:36.580
Oh, it actually runs.

00:21:36.580 --> 00:21:38.350
So we have two devices.

00:21:38.350 --> 00:21:40.110
So in this one
device, we're actually

00:21:40.110 --> 00:21:42.630
running the IMDB application.

00:21:42.630 --> 00:21:46.102
So the IMDB app has been
downloaded from Google Play.

00:21:46.102 --> 00:21:47.310
It's installed in the device.

00:21:47.310 --> 00:21:49.800
So we use the Chrome
Device Management Console.

00:21:49.800 --> 00:21:51.440
Push the app.

00:21:51.440 --> 00:21:53.280
And then once the
app is pushed down,

00:21:53.280 --> 00:21:56.580
the app instantly
runs on the device.

00:21:56.580 --> 00:21:58.150
It can be done remotely.

00:21:58.150 --> 00:22:01.470
And now you have this app
acting as my video kiosk.

00:22:01.470 --> 00:22:04.830
So I can pretty
much run any video.

00:22:04.830 --> 00:22:06.720
Hopefully the network is good.

00:22:06.720 --> 00:22:07.985
But you get the idea.

00:22:07.985 --> 00:22:08.610
So it does run.

00:22:13.501 --> 00:22:14.542
I'm going to skip the ad.

00:22:17.260 --> 00:22:20.207
But this is a completely locked
down, immersive experience.

00:22:20.207 --> 00:22:21.040
So it's locked down.

00:22:21.040 --> 00:22:22.750
And it's running an Android app.

00:22:22.750 --> 00:22:26.080
The second example is we
selected an app, which

00:22:26.080 --> 00:22:28.720
is used by the Hyatt Hotels.

00:22:28.720 --> 00:22:30.820
So it's a Hyatt Regency app.

00:22:30.820 --> 00:22:33.190
It's used in their rooms.

00:22:33.190 --> 00:22:36.010
It's an in-room
controller app, so

00:22:36.010 --> 00:22:39.690
that every guest who is
in the hotel premises,

00:22:39.690 --> 00:22:44.610
they have this device that is
sitting by their bed stand.

00:22:44.610 --> 00:22:48.430
And they can actually
access assets and properties

00:22:48.430 --> 00:22:50.090
of the hotel.

00:22:50.090 --> 00:22:53.380
And this is, again, an Android
app that is just downloaded

00:22:53.380 --> 00:22:56.760
and now running on this
Chromebase, Chrome OS device.

00:22:56.760 --> 00:22:58.240
So these are two good examples.

00:22:58.240 --> 00:23:01.840
And you can do the same thing
with the Chromebox Mini.

00:23:01.840 --> 00:23:04.020
You can pretty much power
this with any big display.

00:23:04.020 --> 00:23:06.640
It could be a display
of this, a huge display.

00:23:06.640 --> 00:23:08.849
And you can then run
Android apps as well.

00:23:08.849 --> 00:23:09.640
So that's our goal.

00:23:16.750 --> 00:23:20.530
And lastly deployment
is a huge consideration

00:23:20.530 --> 00:23:23.080
when you're selecting any of
these different solutions,

00:23:23.080 --> 00:23:25.420
whether it's Chrome or Android.

00:23:25.420 --> 00:23:28.570
With Chrome, we have really
made the deployment process

00:23:28.570 --> 00:23:30.100
to be fairly simple.

00:23:30.100 --> 00:23:33.376
So it's really as simple
as getting a Chromebox,

00:23:33.376 --> 00:23:35.000
connecting it to a
screen, whether it's

00:23:35.000 --> 00:23:39.290
an HDMI port or a display port,
opening up the Chrome Device

00:23:39.290 --> 00:23:42.830
Management Console on a laptop,
configuring the policies,

00:23:42.830 --> 00:23:44.000
pushing it down.

00:23:44.000 --> 00:23:46.190
And then really you
have a digital sign.

00:23:46.190 --> 00:23:48.659
So the app is already
pushed onto the device.

00:23:48.659 --> 00:23:50.450
And then you have
content that is changing.

00:23:50.450 --> 00:23:54.110
And it's reflecting based
on who the audience is.

00:23:54.110 --> 00:23:57.470
In addition today
we're also announcing

00:23:57.470 --> 00:24:00.440
support for Chrome Kiosk API.

00:24:00.440 --> 00:24:03.650
So these APIs would really
allow third party partners

00:24:03.650 --> 00:24:07.370
to build custom solutions on
top of the Chrome Management

00:24:07.370 --> 00:24:08.240
Console.

00:24:08.240 --> 00:24:12.410
So you can now access
specific Chrome policies

00:24:12.410 --> 00:24:15.980
to control things like
reboots or remote commands.

00:24:15.980 --> 00:24:19.130
So this is something that
we also have available.

00:24:19.130 --> 00:24:20.960
And lastly, last but
not the least, this

00:24:20.960 --> 00:24:23.310
is not the most exciting
feature is actually.

00:24:23.310 --> 00:24:25.700
One of the most
common feedback we

00:24:25.700 --> 00:24:30.260
get from our partners
and our customers

00:24:30.260 --> 00:24:34.250
is that the process of signing
up and purchasing a Chrome

00:24:34.250 --> 00:24:37.580
Kiosk is very complicated today.

00:24:37.580 --> 00:24:40.280
You have to do a complex
mechanism of domain

00:24:40.280 --> 00:24:42.620
registration, verification.

00:24:42.620 --> 00:24:43.770
You don't own the domain.

00:24:43.770 --> 00:24:45.080
You're not an IT administrator.

00:24:45.080 --> 00:24:47.062
You don't own the DNS
records for the domain.

00:24:47.062 --> 00:24:48.520
So it's a very
complicated process.

00:24:48.520 --> 00:24:52.410
So our goal is we want to
make the process for anybody,

00:24:52.410 --> 00:24:55.510
whether it's a mom and pop
shop, a flower shop owner,

00:24:55.510 --> 00:24:58.970
or it's a small team
within a huge enterprise,

00:24:58.970 --> 00:25:04.250
to be able to very easily
sign up for a Chrome Kiosk.

00:25:04.250 --> 00:25:07.352
So these should just
provide three fields.

00:25:07.352 --> 00:25:09.560
They need to provide their
name, their email address,

00:25:09.560 --> 00:25:10.730
and their phone number.

00:25:10.730 --> 00:25:12.620
So once they provide
these three fields,

00:25:12.620 --> 00:25:14.870
they will automatically be
able to, with a quick email

00:25:14.870 --> 00:25:17.090
verification and
SMS verification,

00:25:17.090 --> 00:25:22.250
they will be able to instantly
access a web-based console.

00:25:22.250 --> 00:25:25.580
And then two trial licenses
will be given to them so

00:25:25.580 --> 00:25:26.960
that they can manage devices.

00:25:26.960 --> 00:25:28.580
And they can then purchase more.

00:25:28.580 --> 00:25:31.920
So we'll do a demo
of this as well.

00:25:31.920 --> 00:25:35.490
